Z||000000||firstfiero||12-20-2001||07:22 AM||||    Let's see if you guys our as good as I know you are.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm going to have a mechanic fix my car because I just don't have time. He hasn't gotten a chance to look at it yet so let's see if you can tell me what's wrong befor he can.<BR>     <BR>    Here's goes.... yesterday I got on it to pass someone and when I pushed in the clutch to hit second about half way down suddenly the tension left and it went to the floor. I got it in second and barely made it into the 3rd...it was tough...but couldn't shift to forth and by the time I pulled it off the road a few minutes later I couldn't get it into any gear. When I got out of the car I looked under neath and some kind of fresh fluid was laying on some hose lines and heat sheild. Could I have just blown some kind of hydraulic hose for the clutch! The clutch never slips and It's only about 25 thousand miles old. My best friend had this car befor me, he's the one who put in the clutch , but he drove like an old man so I know he wasn't rough on it! What do you guys think?<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indyrestoguy_JR||12-20-2001||07:24 AM||||Bad line.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tesmith66||12-20-2001||07:47 AM||||Either the line or the fitting at the slave cylinder.<P>Make sure the mechanic knows how to bleed a Fiero clutch. Go to either Archie's or Ed Parks' sites and get their procedures and give them to your mechanic. If he's never bled a Fiero clutch, he's in for a wild ride...<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||12-20-2001||07:54 AM||||   He's had fiero's befor. I think you guys are right the other thing that I didn't tell you is I heard metal scraping. When a friend got their I had him push in the clutch and you could see where the line runs into the slave cylinder looked like it broke loose and every time you pushed in the clutch it would move and cause the heat shield to scrape against another heat sheild. Oh well...I drive her like I stole and the police are after me every day...got to expect it to breack down every now and then.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
